WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.169 --> 00:00:01.660
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:09.420
In 1978 paleoanthropologist Andrew Hill was
throwing shit at his colleague when he discovered

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:15.700
one of the most important pieces of evidence
to ever support the theory of evolution.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:21.330
Hill and his colleague were avoiding doing
work by throwing elephant dung at each other

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.910
at an archeological site in Tanzania.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.720
Hill dove towards the ground to narrowly avoid
a large dung projectile hitting him in the

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:29.720
face.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:36.710
As he slammed into the ground he noticed something
peculiar within the dirt of the excavation

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.690
site, a trail of footprints.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:45.920
These incredible footprints that had been
perfectly preserved by hardened volcanic ash

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.809
were found to be 3.6 million years old.

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:54.879
They had been made by some of the very first
upright-walking hominids.

00:00:54.879 --> 00:01:00.949
Up until Hill's chance discovery the oldest
human footprints we had found were only tens

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:06.859
of thousands of years old. 3.6 million years
ago when these footprints were made, our ancestors

00:01:06.859 --> 00:01:12.850
looked remarkably similar yet so very different,
than modern man.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:18.320
Australopithecus is the name science has given
to the specimens found from this period of

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.840
human's evolutionary timeline.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.750
Australopithecus looked profoundly more apelike.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:29.770
Compared to modern day humans, they had far
smaller brains, a protruding large jaw and

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.390
stubby nose.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.689
The progress mankind has made physically,
in what is relatively, a very small amount

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:38.260
of time, is mind-blowing.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.630
If evolution carries on at this rate I should
have superpowers in no time.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.749
Where's my x-ray vision and superior hindsight?

00:01:46.749 --> 00:01:55.049
But along the way something happened and evolution
was stopped in its tracks.

00:01:55.049 --> 00:02:02.210
Human evolution has progressed so remarkably
fast, Earth is 4.5 billion years old and in

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:09.270
only a tiny 7 million years, which equates
to just 0.15 per cent of Earth's history,

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:15.190
humans have evolved from a primitive apelike
ancestor to a walking, talking, intelligent

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.190
being.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.650
Well, most of us anyway.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:24.420
But this rapid physical and mental change
within our species was caused due to immense

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.930
environmental pressures.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:33.110
For the vast majority of humankind's history
and our ancestor's, we have not been predator's

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:36.879
like we are today, but prey.

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:42.440
Only with the advent of weapons and technological
advancement have we risen to the top of the

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.819
food chain.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:49.260
Many early fossilised human remains have been
found all over the globe that have fatal wounds

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:55.970
made by animals, such as tigers, leopards,
and even by an eagles' talons, as was found

00:02:55.970 --> 00:03:01.819
to be the cause of death of the 2 million
year old "Taung Child" skull.

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:07.769
So both physical and mental adaptation was
necessary for our species' future survival

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:09.420
and prosperity.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.470
Rapid changes had to be made so we were better
equipped both mentally and physically, to

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.610
fend of predators and find food.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:21.470
And so evolution showed no signs of stopping.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:26.610
But then we went and ruined it all by saying
something stupid like "let's build a homogeneous

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.329
civilisation."

00:03:28.329 --> 00:03:36.400
In 3100 BC Mesopotamia was built, the first
human civilisation.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:42.269
Huge advances were made in farming and humans
no longer needed to forage or hunt to survive.

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:48.069
As the centuries have passed we have, on average,
all become wealthier, better medicated and

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:50.640
gained easier access to food.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:57.569
The pressure to adapt to our environment disappeared
and so did the rapid evolutionary progress.

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:03.430
Today not only the fittest and strongest pass
on their genes to the next generation, but

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.129
everybody does.

00:04:05.129 --> 00:04:09.870
This is especially true in the West, with
modern medicine and food at our fingertips

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:15.740
whenever we desire it, even the most stupid
and weakest members of society will pass on

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:21.660
their genes and that they most certainly do,
even if said individuals don't know exactly

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.800
who's genes they have passed on, one only
needs to watch five minutes of Jeremy Kyle

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.510
to understand what I'm talking about.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:34.190
So in developed countries at least, there
is no natural selection anymore.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:39.940
Sir David Attenborough himself said that "We
are the only species to have put a halt to

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.970
natural selection, of its own free will.”

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:50.010
Attenborough predicts that physical evolution
in humans will eventually cease completely

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:56.500
and we will instead go through a process of
cultural evolution, in which we will evolve

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.030
mentally.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:04.040
So whilst survival of the fittest may no longer
hold true, survival of the intelligent certainly

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.350
does.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:09.670
As each generation builds upon the wisdom
of those before them, intellectual growth

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:12.490
will speed up exponentially.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:17.950
Today a person's survival depends not on whether
they can effectively hunt prey but whether

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:22.790
they can secure a good job to buy food for
themselves and their family.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:28.260
It has thus become more important than ever
that people are more intelligent and more

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.450
creative than their peers.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:36.470
There are only so many jobs in the world and
this fierce competition to be the best, climb

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:42.200
the ladder and steal more prestigious jobs
from others has put an evolutionary pressure

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.070
on our minds.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:52.570
The Flynn effect is the observation that over
time average IQ levels have increased, substantially.

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:58.500
Since 1904, when IQ tests were first used,
the average IQ level across the globe has

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:03.650
increased every single year, in a linear fashion.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:09.700
Every few years IQ tests are completely re-written
and intentionally made harder so that the

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:15.030
global average always remains at 100.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:20.810
If you were to take an IQ test from 80 years
ago you would find it significantly easier

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.060
than a modern day test.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:30.280
Human evolution has not stopped, far from
it, but it's goals have changed.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:34.270
Mental acuity is now the next target of natural
selection.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:39.310
So it looks like that X-Ray vision might have
to wait, shame.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:43.660
So we're evolving culturally, although that's
very hard to believe looking at the current

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.530
state of contemporary music.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.900
But what about physically?

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.060
Is this really all we're getting?

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.650
Has humanity peaked ascetically and mechanically?

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:59.480
Well, that may not be entirely the case.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:04.240
It's generally accepted that evolution has
been slowing down since the dawn of human

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.240
civilisation.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:11.800
But we shouldn't be so quick to put a definite
end on physical evolution, after all, mutations

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:17.860
don't occur overnight, they take tens, sometimes
hundreds of thousands of years to take hold.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:26.720
And, if we look really closely, we have actually
changed physically, in recent times.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:32.710
Despite getting more intelligent, over the
past 30,000 years our brains have shrunk,

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:40.280
from an average of 1,500 cubic centimetres
to 1,350 cubic centimetres.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:46.680
Blue eyes are a prime example of evolution,
until just 10,000 years ago, blue eyes did

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.660
not exist, everyone had brown eyes.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:56.870
But 10,000 years ago some unknown patient
zero near the Black Sea developed a genetic

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.500
mutation that turned their eyes blue.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:04.810
They passed down the blue-eyed mutation to
many others and very soon blue eyes became

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:09.470
extremely popular, for an unexpected reason.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:13.430
Blue eyes were an early form of paternity
test.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:18.560
Men would often prefer female partners with
blue eyes because the man would know that

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.800
if his wife had a blue-eyed baby then it was
probably his.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.610
If the baby had brown eyes, then someone had
been a little naughty.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:32.740
Studies have shown that most men find blue
eyes more attractive than brown and it's thought

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:38.069
that this unreliable historical paternity
test could be the reason.

00:08:38.069 --> 00:08:42.690
Of course we now know that eye colour genes
can be passed down through several family

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:48.180
generations and even if both parents have
blue eyes, it's still possible for them to

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:50.810
give birth to a brown-eyed baby.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:57.230
So I imagine throughout history a lot of unlucky
women were incorrectly accused of cheating.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:03.120
But surely one of the best ways we have evolved
in modern times is that humans have become

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.180
naturally more resistant to diseases.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:12.720
Even when we have food on the table and good
healthcare there is one environmental pressure

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.589
that hasn't left us alone since the dawn of
time.

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:22.560
One of the world's biggest killers, malaria.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:28.470
Over one million people die from malaria each
year, mostly in sub-saharan Africa.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:37.181
But in 2007 a study found a group of 1,800,
previously undiscovered genes that have only

00:09:37.181 --> 00:09:41.930
become prevalent in humans in the past 40,000
years.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:47.540
These genes make us more resistant to various
diseases, such as tuberculosis, leprosy and

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.970
even malaria.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:54.779
And it's predicted that these genes will only
become stronger and more prevalent within

00:09:54.779 --> 00:09:58.020
the human race in the future.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:03.350
Evolution has conquered hunger, and within
the next few hundred millennia we may even

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:13.279
conquer disease, for good.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:20.739
Thanks for watching.

